<title>UK: Sonatrach cuts Feb LPG price to $335/$290 a tonne.</title>
<headline>Sonatrach cuts Feb LPG price to $335/$290 a tonne.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algerian state oil and gas company Sonatrach has cut its official posted prices for Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) for February to $335 a tonne for propane and $290 a tonne for butane.</p>
<p>This is a cut of $30 a tonne in both cases, from $365 a tonne and $330 a tonne in January.</p>
<p>The prices apply to cargoes loading at Bethioua. Cargoes loading at Arzew or Skikda carry a premium of $7 a tonne.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
